  "notes": "Web 414 \u2014 DISPATCH-NAVIGATE-NO-DESTINATION (Nov 11, 2026). Tapping Navigate on the active dispatch opened the Navigator at his position with no destination and no route. Convicted cause, in the dispatch pin resolution only: the Nov 11 Aecon Trans dispatch carried its pins only in its notes \u2014 'Go Empty To: (51.1225089, -114.0122197)' with its Maps link and 'Hauling To: (51.3078889, -114.0369722)' with its link \u2014 typed in when the dispatch was entered, so the record's lat/lng fields were never set on either stored copy, and dspRecordPin read only those fields before the tap fell through to the site-text search. The fix: the resolver now reads the record's own notes as its last resort \u2014 the pin the notes label 'Go Empty To' (the coordinate pair after the label, in the pair or the Maps link after it, never past the 'Hauling To' label), the tapped copy's notes before the other copy's; a stored pin on either copy still outranks the notes, and an unlabelled pair in the notes is not a pin. Load counting, the Dump-only door and every other screen are untouched. Bench: tools/dispatch-navnotes-v414-test.js \u2014 on web 413 the morning's tap handed the Navigator a text query with no coordinates and recorded no visit; on 414 the tap sets the destination to the Go Empty pin exactly and records the work navigation, the stored-pin and cross-copy guards hold, and Hauling-only or unlabelled notes still fall through with no coordinates. Verdict owed in Asjad's hands: Navigate on a dispatch whose pins sit in its notes must start the route to the Go Empty pin.",
